ven-names>RN</given-names></name><name><surname>Valiyaveettil</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Alkhalil</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ockenhouse</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name><name><surname>Gowda</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of proteoglycans of human placenta and identification of unique chondroitin sulfate proteoglycans of the intervillous spaces that mediate the adherence of <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic>-infected erythrocytes to the placenta.</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><year>2000</year><volume>275</volume><fpage>40344</fpage><lpage>40356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11005814</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muthusamy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Structural characterization of the bovine tracheal chondroitin sulfate chains and binding of <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic>-infected erythrocytes.</article-title><source>Glycobiology</source><year>2004</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>635</fpage><lpage>645</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15044390</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R24"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Higgins</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The structure of a chondroitin sulphate-binding domain important in placental malaria.</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><day>11</day><month>6</month><year>2008</year><comment>published online, doi:10.1074/jbc.C8000086200</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="R25"><label>25</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Heparin-induced <italic>cis</italic>- and <italic>trans</italic>-dimerization modes of the thrombospondin-1 N-terminal domain.</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><year>2008</year><volume>283</volume><fpage>3932</fpage><lpage>3941</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18065761</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R26"><label>26</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The structures of the thrombospondin-1 N-terminal domain and its complex with a synthetic pentameric heparin.</article-title><source>Structure</source><year>2006</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16407063</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R27"><label>27</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gamain</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Identification of a 67-amino-acid region of the <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic> variant surface antigen that binds chondroitin sulphate A and elicits antibodies reactive with the surface of placental isolates.</article-title><source>Mol. Microbiol</source><year>2004</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>445</fpage><lpage>455</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15228526</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R28"><label>28</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahlback</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Epitope mapping and topographic analysis of VAR2CSA DBL3X involved in <italic>P. falciparum</italic> placental sequestration.</article-title><source>PLoS Pathog</source><year>2006</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>e124</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17112315</pub-id></element-citation><